Runtime: CommandLine.arguments without /proc/self/maps (musl).

What: the musl argv grabber locates the main thread's stack via /proc/self/maps
and walks back from `environ`. When the stack bounds are unknown it now walks
down from environ[-1] == NULL, counting slots until the slot value equals the
count (argc), i.e. it relies on the initial stack layout only.
Why: without a readable /proc/self/maps CommandLine.arguments was empty and
programs indexing arguments[0] (swift-driver among them) trapped.
Upstream: plausible; the fallback is only reached where the result used to be
an empty array.

Apply inside the `swift` repository: git apply <this file>
---
diff --git a/stdlib/public/CommandLineSupport/CommandLine.cpp b/stdlib/public/CommandLineSupport/CommandLine.cpp
--- a/stdlib/public/CommandLineSupport/CommandLine.cpp
+++ b/stdlib/public/CommandLineSupport/CommandLine.cpp
@@ -322,7 +322,32 @@
 // Find argv by walking backwards from environ
 void ArgvGrabber::findArgv(ArgvGrabber::stack stack) {
   if (!stack.base) {
-    ARGVDEBUG("no stack\n");
+    // /proc/self/maps could not be read (no procfs, sandboxes, emulators), so
+    // the stack bounds are unknown.  Rely on the initial process stack layout
+    // instead:
+    //
+    //     argc, argv[0] ... argv[argc - 1], NULL, envp[0] ...
+    //
+    // Walk down from the NULL that terminates argv, counting entries, until
+    // the slot whose value equals the number of entries seen: that is argc.
+    // Every entry before it must look like a pointer into the string area
+    // above envp, otherwise `environ` no longer points at the initial stack
+    // and we give up rather than read arbitrary memory.
+    ARGVDEBUG("no stack; using the initial stack layout\n");
+    char **initialEnvp = environ;
+    if (!initialEnvp || initialEnvp[-1] != nullptr)
+      return;
+
+    char **slot = initialEnvp - 2;
+    for (intptr_t count = 0; count < (1 << 20); ++count, --slot) {
+      if ((intptr_t)*slot == count) {
+        argc = (int)count;
+        argv = slot + 1;
+        return;
+      }
+      if ((void *)*slot <= (void *)initialEnvp)
+        return;
+    }
     return;
   }
 
